1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,680
Before we check out there's one key word that I haven't talked about yet.
结账前，还有一个关键词我没谈到。

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:12,640
And we need to talk about it can you guess what it is it's the word grocery grocery store that's where I'm at.
我们需要讲讲它。你能猜到是什么吗？就是 grocery。grocery store，就是我现在所在的地方。

3
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,870
And I'm buying groceries.
而我正在买 groceries，也就是食品杂货。

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:21,240
There's two different pronunciations for this and it's just a regional difference or a personal preference.
这个词有两种发音，只是地区差异或个人偏好。

5
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:26,990
You can say grocery with an s sound in the middle.
你可以在单词中间发 s 的音，grocery。

6
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:40,640
Grocery grocery but for me I say gry with a sh sound in the middle grocery store grocery store.
grocery。但我会在中间发 sh 的音，grocery store，grocery store。

7
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:42,599
Both of these options are correct.
这两种说法都正确。

8
00:00:42,599 --> 00:00:45,880
And it just depends on what you feel the most comfortable saying.
只取决于你说哪一种更自在。

9
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:52,520
So you could say I'm at the grocery store or I'm at the grocery store.
所以你可以说我在 grocery store，或者我在 grocery store。

10
00:00:52,520 --> 00:00:58,800
Store I'm buying groceries or I'm buying groceries.
我正在买 groceries，或者我正在买 groceries。

11
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,599
Both of these are beautiful very natural.
这两种说法都很好，也都很自然。

12
00:01:01,599 --> 00:01:08,230
And it's the most common expression that you're going to hear in the us when we talk about a store where you buy food.
在美国，谈到买食品的商店，这是最常听到的表达。

13
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,320
It's the grocery store.
就是 grocery store。

14
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:12,880
Now it's time to check out.
现在该结账了。

15
00:01:12,880 --> 00:01:16,320
We can use this word as a noun or a verb.
这个词可以当名词，也可以当动词。

16
00:01:16,320 --> 00:01:21,440
Let's checkout or let's go to the checkout.
可以说，让我们结账；也可以说，让我们去结账处。

17
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:26,479
You can also say the checkout counter let's go to the checkout counter.
还可以说 checkout counter。我们去收银台吧。

18
00:01:26,479 --> 00:01:29,839
I need to buy the things that I put in my cart.
我需要把放在购物车里的东西买下来。

19
00:01:29,839 --> 00:01:34,839
Let's check out it's time to check out at the checkout counter.
结账吧，该在收银台结账了。

20
00:01:34,839 --> 00:01:40,920
Watch out because there are a lot of snacks and junk food waiting for you.
注意，那里有很多零食和她称为垃圾食品的东西在等着你。

21
00:01:40,920 --> 00:01:45,599
The grocery store wants you to splurge and buy these things.
商店希望你多花一点钱，把这些东西买下来。

22
00:01:45,599 --> 00:01:50,880
For me I try to avoid them it's always unhealthy not really a good choice.
我会尽量避开；她觉得这些总是不健康，并非好的选择。

23
00:01:50,880 --> 00:01:54,360
But this is here to make a last minute purchase.
不过，这些东西摆在这里，就是为了让人临时起意购买。

24
00:01:54,360 --> 00:02:01,560
I want to know in your country are there a lot of snacks and junk food options waiting at the checkout.
我想知道，在你们国家，结账处是不是也有很多零食和垃圾食品可选？

25
00:02:01,560 --> 00:02:03,709
I think this is kind of common around the world.
我觉得这种现象在世界各地似乎都挺常见。

26
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:07,440
But let me know in the comments if this happens in your country.
但如果你们国家也有这种情况，请在评论里告诉我。

27
00:02:07,440 --> 00:02:14,120
Now I'm asking the kind checkout lady if I have her permission to film while I'm checking out.
现在，我正在问这位亲切的收银员，是否允许我在结账时拍摄。

28
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:19,680
I wanted to give you this experience to see the final step at the grocery store.
我想让你有这种体验，看到超市购物的最后一步。

29
00:02:19,680 --> 00:02:30,839
Well I forgot all of my bags today so I can I can help to check out too um let's do paper.
今天我忘了把自己的袋子带来，所以我可以……我也可以帮着结账。嗯，用纸袋吧。

30
00:02:30,839 --> 00:02:34,589
Now all of the items are going down the conveyor belt.
现在，所有商品都在传送带上向前移动。

31
00:02:34,599 --> 00:02:39,279
And the checkout lady is scanning them while I put them in my bag.
收银员一边扫描商品，我一边把它们装进袋子。

32
00:02:39,279 --> 00:02:49,320
I usually bring my own bags but this day I was so focused on filming I totally forgot so I chose to get paper bags.
我通常会自己带袋子，但这一天太专注于拍摄，完全忘了，所以选了纸袋。

33
00:02:49,320 --> 00:02:53,000
I can compost the paper bags in my gard garden.
我可以把纸袋放进花园里做堆肥。

34
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:59,599
But you might choose to get a plastic bag because you can reuse them as a trash bag in your house.
你也可能选塑料袋，因为可以在家里重复利用，当作垃圾袋。

35
00:02:59,599 --> 00:03:03,279
It's time to pay for all of these groceries.
现在该为这些食品杂货付款了。

36
00:03:03,279 --> 00:03:08,000
I'm scanning my membership card so that I can get a few discounts.
我正在扫描会员卡，这样可以享受一些折扣。

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:11,960
And she asks me if I want to use cash or credit.
她问我想用现金还是信用卡。

38
00:03:11,960 --> 00:03:17,760
Or she might say cash or card and you can choose which one.
她也可能说 cash or card，你可以选择其中一种。

39
00:03:17,760 --> 00:03:26,479
Thank you thanks you too I appreciate your help yes bye.
谢谢。谢谢你，你也是。感谢你的帮助。好的，再见。

40
00:03:26,479 --> 00:03:30,800
Now I go out through the automatic doors like magic.
接着，我穿过自动门走出去，像变魔术一样。

41
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:36,479
And load the groceries in the car I load the groceries in the car.
然后把食品杂货装上车，把它们装进车里。

42
00:03:36,479 --> 00:03:40,279
And then at home I will unload the groceries.
回到家后，我会把这些食品杂货卸下来。
